nicotine based e-cigarettes are NOT responsible for the new wave of lung disorders being reported by mass media outlets and shared by millions on social media.

the common contributing link between these cases are the use of black market thc cartridges, which are vaporized using the same hardware and delivery mechanism as the more common nicotine based e-cigarettes .

often times, these cartridges are produced to be sold legally in states that have legitimate medical marijuana programs. this means, however, that the products being sold are subject to health standards which require extensive lab testing. when a batch of (already produced) cartridges are not approved to be sold, the producer is stuck with useless product. many of these rejected cartridges are instead sold in states where there is no legal option to buy cannabis.

this, in addition to more nefarious black market operations where unsafe additives are used to reduce the production costs of their product, explains why the “mysterious vaping illness” has occurred ONLY in states where marijuana use remains strictly illegal.

let’s be clear: using e-cigarettes is not good for you. but, conflating the use of black market thc cartridges with vaporizing nicotine is simply a manipulative tactic to create scary headlines.

